# Wellness Room Designer - environment variables
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) for local Vite dev.
# Set the SERVER vars (anything WITHOUT `VITE_`) in the Vercel project
# Environment Variables tab - NEVER in `.env.local` (Vite leaks anything
# prefixed `VITE_` into the bundle, and `.env.local` may get pulled by
# accident on a Vercel preview build).

# --- Client -----------------------------------------------------------
# Public - safe to ship in the JS bundle. Used by @stripe/stripe-js.
VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --- Server (Vercel project env vars) ---------------------------------
# Stripe secret API key - used by /api/create-checkout-session.
# `sk_test_...` for sandbox, `sk_live_...` once Vic verifies the account.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# Stripe webhook signing secret - used by /api/stripe-webhook to verify
# every event. Grab from Stripe Dashboard -> Developers -> Webhooks ->
# your endpoint -> "Signing secret".
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Resend transactional email - needed for order confirmation +
# Vic-alert emails sent from /api/stripe-webhook. Unset = dry-run
# (payload printed to function logs, no real send).
# Resend dashboard -> API Keys.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
